Isn't this really the key.  The main reason the fighter types
are easiest in the beginning isn't because they fight so well;
it's because they start with more hit points (and often better
AC), and their hit points increase faster.  And a lot of hit
points (and a good AC) is good insurance against a lot of what
can kill you early.  Roles without the hit points and the AC
have to be more careful, and fall more easily prey to
accidental encounters.

(Once you get past the start, of course, the issues change.
Once you've found mithral, plus boots and helmut from dwarves in
the mines, your initial AC becomes less important, for example.
And a couple a hundred hit points mean less than reflection when
you encounter a black dragon.)

